Z||000000||87ECO5||06-05-2000||09:35 AM||||I've never been in this situation before so I'm looking for help.<P>I've got a parts car that I need to get rid of.  Do I have to make arrangements with a junk yard first, or can I just have it towed someplace and dropped off?  Also, it's going to be pretty bare in regards to suspension parts (I'll be removing the wheels, tires, lower control arms, sway bar, springs, etc.).  What kind of problems with this cause me as far as hauling it to the junkyard?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||06-05-2000||10:03 AM||||Look for one of those places that boasts "We buy junk cars"  They may not give you any money for it, but they will take it off your hands.  If you dont know about any of those places in your area, call a junkyard and ask them who hauls off cars that are "mechanically challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-05-2000||10:14 AM||||Scott--Try Art's in Middletown.  They're on Oxford-State Rd.  1-800-404-7133 or (513)424-2733  I'm pretty sure they can help you out.  Seems like I remember a car on one of their trucks last time I was there with no wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||06-05-2000||03:15 PM||||Good suggestion, Monkeyman.  I just got off of the phone with them.  They'll be coming by on Thursday to get it.<P>Here's a list of stuff I'm going to try to pull from it before then:<P>87ECO5 - wheels and tires<BR>2M4 Dale - liner bolts<BR>Monkeyman - front sway bar<BR>ChadMan - radiator, brake master cylinder<BR>redfiero - body panels???<BR>william_thorniii - lower control arms<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 06-05-2000).]||||reg||1
